course: dictionary
lesson: 2238
title: Short words with long names
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are shortened so they are quicker to say and write. CPR is an abbreviation: each letter stands for a longer phrase. The sentence gives you the full name straight after the short word: «CPR, cardiopulmonary resuscitation, means pressing hard and fast on the middle of the chest.»
explain: Look for clues around the short word. The writer often gives the full name next to it, or describes what it is. Here the description tells you what CPR does: it keeps blood moving when the heart has stopped. So CPR is a way of helping someone, not a thing you can hold.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The call handler can talk anyone through cardiopulmonary resuscitation» still makes sense, so you have understood it. Remember that CPR is said as three letters, not as one word.
fact: CPR is an abbreviation: it stands for cardiopulmonary resuscitation.
fact: CPR is said as three letters: «C-P-R».
fact: CPR is first aid for someone whose heart has stopped and who is not breathing.
fact: CPR means pushing hard and fast on the middle of the chest, sometimes with rescue breaths.
fact: CPR can keep blood moving to the brain until an ambulance arrives. Emergency numbers: 999 (UK and Ireland), 911 (USA and Canada), 000 (Australia), 111 (New Zealand).
exercise: «CPR, cardiopulmonary resuscitation, means pressing hard and fast on the middle of the chest.» What does CPR stand for? | central public rescue | cardiac pressure routine | car park road | *cardiopulmonary resuscitation
exercise: How do you say CPR? | Crisp, like the snack | Cap, like a hat | Copper, like the metal | *C-P-R, as three letters
exercise: What is CPR used for? | Stopping a nosebleed | *First aid when someone's heart has stopped and they are not breathing | Lifting heavy shopping | Cooling down after running a race
test: The sentence says the call handler «can talk anyone through it». What does this suggest? | *Someone on the phone can give step-by-step instructions | Nobody can help until the next day | The call handler does all the CPR alone, with no help | The phone call must be ended straight away
test: Which emergency number is used in Australia? | 999 | 911 | 111 | *000
exam: What is the main aim of CPR? | *To keep blood moving to the brain until help arrives | To make the person fall asleep | To cool the person down quickly | To check how tall someone is
